### Using JAXB to Serialize and Deserialize XML in Java

JAXB (Java Architecture for XML Binding) is a tool used to convert between XML data and Java objects. It allows you to define classes that represent your XML structure, and then use those classes to serialize and deserialize XML data.

#### Step 1: Define Your Java Classes

To use JAXB, you need to define Java classes that represent the XML structure you want to serialize and deserialize. For example:

```java
import javax.xml.bind.annotation.XmlRootElement;

@XmlRootElement(name = "example")
public class Example {
    private String value;

    public String getValue() {
        return value;
    }

    public void setValue(String value) {
        this.value = value;
    }
}
```

#### Step 2: Create a JAXB Context

To use JAXB, you need to create a JAXB context that knows about your Java classes. You can do this by creating a `JAXBContext` object:

```java
import javax.xml.bind.JAXBContext;

public class JAXBUtil {
    public static JAXBElement<String> getJAXBElement(String value) {
        return new JAXBElement<>(value, String.class, null);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) throws JAXBException {
        // Create a new XML string
        String xmlString = "<example>example</example>";

        // Deserialize the XML into a Java object
        JAXBContext context = JAXBContext.newInstance(Example.class);
        Unmarshaller unmarshaller = context.createUnmarshaller();
        Example example = (Example) unmarshaller.unmarshal(xmlString);

        // Print the value of the example object
        System.out.println(example.getValue());

        // Serialize the Java object back into an XML string
        Marshaller marshaller = context.createMarshaller();
        marshaller.setSchema(new Schema());
        Example newExample = new Example("example");
        marshaller.marshal(newExample, System.out);
    }
}
```

#### Step 3: Use JAXB to Serialize and Deserialize Data

Once you have a JAXB context, you can use it to serialize and deserialize data. For example:

```java
